  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p style="color: var(--muted)"><em>Last updated: November 2026</em></p>

  <p>
    By accessing or using the Highway Old Students' Association (HOSA) website,
    you agree to these Terms of Service, which are governed by the HOSA
    Constitution and applicable laws of the Republic of Uganda. If you do not
    agree, please do not register or use the platform.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Eligibility and Membership</h2>

  <p>
    Membership of HOSA is governed by its Constitution and is categorized as
    Ordinary, Life or Honorary membership.
  </p>

  <p>
    Applicants must provide accurate and complete information when registering.
    Applicants seeking Ordinary Membership must provide relevant academic and
    school history for membership verification.
  </p>

  <p>
    Submitting an application does not automatically grant membership.
    Applications are subject to review and approval by authorized HOSA
    administrators in accordance with the Constitution and applicable membership
    procedures.
  </p>

  <p>
    Members are expected to meet the applicable registration and annual
    subscription obligations determined by the authorized HOSA organs. Honorary
    members acknowledge that their membership rights, including voting rights,
    are governed by the Constitution.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Acceptable Use</h2>

  <p>You agree not to:</p>

  <ul>
    <li>Harass, threaten, intimidate or defame other members.</li>
    <li>Publish fraudulent jobs, scams or misleading opportunities.</li>
    <li>
      Solicit money from members without prior approval from the Executive
      Committee or other authorized HOSA organ.
    </li>
    <li>Impersonate another person or create fraudulent accounts.</li>
    <li>
      Use the platform to promote hate speech, discrimination or unlawful
      activities.
    </li>
    <li>
      Access, modify or interfere with accounts, information or platform
      resources without authorization.
    </li>
    <li>Misuse members' personal information or contact details.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Content You Post</h2>

  <p>
    You retain ownership of content you submit or publish through the platform,
    including stories, jobs, regional reports, business information and other
    contributions.
  </p>

  <p>
    By submitting content, you grant HOSA a non-exclusive license to store,
    reproduce and display that content for purposes connected with operating the
    Association and its platform.
  </p>

  <p>
    All submissions are subject to review and moderation by authorized HOSA
    officers. You are responsible for ensuring that content you submit is
    accurate, lawful and does not infringe the rights of others.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Financial Obligations</h2>

  <p>
    Members must meet applicable registration fees, annual subscriptions and
    other approved financial obligations as determined in accordance with the
    HOSA Constitution and decisions of the authorized Association organs.
  </p>

  <p>
    The platform may record contributions, subscriptions and payment information
    for verification, reconciliation and accountability. Members should follow
    the officially communicated payment procedures and retain appropriate
    evidence of payment.
  </p>

  <p>
    Failure to meet applicable financial obligations may affect certain
    membership privileges, including voting eligibility at the General Assembly,
    where provided for by the Constitution. Any restriction must be administered
    in accordance with the Constitution and applicable procedures.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Collective Investment and Development Schemes (CIDS)</h2>

  <p>
    The platform may provide information and opportunities relating to
    Collective Investment and Development Schemes (CIDS). Such schemes belong to
    their subscribing members and are not automatically owned or operated by
    HOSA.
  </p>

  <p>
    HOSA may provide oversight or coordination within the scope of its
    authorized responsibilities but does not guarantee investment returns or the
    financial performance of any scheme.
  </p>

  <p>
    Participation is voluntary. Members are responsible for evaluating
    investment decisions and understanding the associated financial risks before
    committing funds.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Moderation and Discipline</h2>

  <p>
    HOSA moderators and authorized officers may review, edit, restrict or remove
    content that violates these Terms of Service, the HOSA Constitution or
    applicable laws.
  </p>

  <p>
    Serious misconduct, repeated violations or actions that bring the
    Association into disrepute may be referred to the independent Disciplinary
    Committee in accordance with Article 3.5 of the Constitution.
  </p>

  <p>
    Membership suspension, disciplinary action or termination must follow the
    applicable constitutional provisions and established procedures.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Dispute Resolution</h2>

  <p>
    Disputes arising from the use of the platform or interactions between
    members should initially be addressed through the appropriate HOSA
    governance and dispute-resolution procedures.
  </p>

  <p>
    Where a dispute cannot be resolved through the Association's applicable
    procedures, the parties may pursue remedies available under the laws of the
    Republic of Uganda.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Disclaimer</h2>

  <p>
    HOSA does not guarantee the accuracy, completeness or reliability of jobs,
    business opportunities, mentorship advice, investment information or other
    content published by members.
  </p>

  <p>
    HOSA is not responsible for independent transactions or interactions between
    members. Members should exercise appropriate judgment, particularly when
    sharing personal information, entering financial arrangements or
    participating in investment activities.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Changes to These Terms</h2>

  <p>
    HOSA may update these Terms of Service to reflect amendments to its
    Constitution, changes in Association operations or changes in applicable
    laws.
  </p>

  <p>
    Material changes will be communicated through appropriate HOSA channels.
    Where renewed acceptance is required, members will be asked to accept the
    revised terms.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Contact</h2>

  <p>
    For questions or concerns about these Terms of Service, contact the HOSA
    Secretariat at
    <a href="mailto:support@hosa-uganda.org">support@hosa-uganda.org</a>.
  </p>
